    "classification": "PRESENT",
    "entry_guards": [
      "branch 3 requires positive signed surface flux over material frost",
      "`thaw_fine_top_with_resistance_feedback` returns early when surface_temp_c <= 0",
      "`top_flux_w_m2 = surface_temp_c / thaw_surface_heat_path(...)` must be positive",
      "a fine layer must contain frozen depth and ice mass before `thaw_fine_top_step` consumes energy"
    ],
    "important_metric_distinction": "`frdp` is the bottom extent of the frozen domain. `thdp` is the thawed surface cap above a frozen segment. Top-front retreat may increase `thdp` without reducing `frdp` on the same day.",
    "summary": "A top-down thaw path exists. `select_frost_branch` chooses branch 3 when signed surface flux is positive over an existing frozen column, `apply_active_frost_thaw_step` calls `thaw_fine_top_with_resistance_feedback`, and `thaw_fine_top_step` reduces fine-layer `slfsd_m`/`slsic_m` from the surface downward."
